# ARQEDIA front-end build configuration.
#
# Copy this file to ui/.env and fill it in. ui/.env is git-ignored and must
# stay that way; this example is committed and must never hold a real token.
#
# Both variables are REQUIRED. There is no default: a build without them
# fails, deliberately, rather than producing a bundle pointed at the wrong
# Paddle account. The pair must agree - sandbox takes a test_ token, and
# production takes a live_ one - and the build refuses a mismatch.
#
# The client-side token is public by Paddle's own documentation: "safe to
# publish". The API key and the webhook secret are NOT, and never appear
# here or anywhere else in this directory - they live in AWS Secrets Manager
# and are read by the Lambda (decision record item 1).

# sandbox | production
VITE_PADDLE_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox

# test_... for sandbox, live_... for production.
# Paddle > Developer tools > Authentication > Client-side tokens.
VITE_PADDLE_TOKEN=test_replace_me
